---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="mb-6 font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white">
        LED-Based Countdown Timer
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Project Overview</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral">Together with my teammate, I designed and built a four-digit countdown timer for our Circuits and Electronics course. The project used custom 7-segment LED displays (each segment assembled from discrete LEDs), controlled by an Arduino Uno, with a potentiometer for time adjustment and a buzzer for alerts.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Key Features</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Custom four-digit display built from individual LEDs</li>
          <li>Arduino Uno for countdown logic and display multiplexing</li>
          <li>Buzzer alarms at halfway, one-minute remaining, and countdown completion</li>
          <li>Potentiometer input for precise time setting</li>
          <li>Custom circuit with transistors and capacitors for efficient multiplexing and signal smoothing</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Technical Implementation</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Multiplexing with NPN transistors to drive four LED digits and a colon indicator</li>
          <li>Resistor-based current regulation for LED brightness and safety (470 Ω per segment, 1 kΩ at transistor bases)</li>
          <li>Analog input processing from a 10 kΩ potentiometer for user-controlled time settings</li>
          <li>PWM control for buzzer signaling</li>
          <li>Power regulation with a transformer, LM7805 voltage regulator, and smoothing capacitors (100 µF, 470 µF)</li>
          <li>Arduino C++ programming for countdown logic, LED digit rendering, and alert management</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Challenges & Improvements</h2>
        <ul class="text-neutral list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Breadboard wiring complexity: multiplexing required careful layout to avoid messy bundling.</li>
          <li>LED availability: limited red and green LEDs led us to substitute with yellow.</li>
          <li>Flickering issues: mitigated by increasing capacitor sizes for better voltage stability.</li>
          <li>Future improvements include designing a custom PCB for portability, better aesthetics, and reduced wiring complexity.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <a href="https://drive.com" target="_blank" class="rounded-full bg-primary px-8 py-4 text-white font-medium hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors after:ml-2 after:content-[url(/external.svg)]">
          View Demo Video
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>